---
/**
 * On demand, and that is the whole fix for the prerendered pages.
 *
 * **A static `404.html` is answered by Cloudflare before the worker runs.**
 * That is what took out every public page: a request for `/guides/` matched
 * no asset, Pages served this file, and the middleware — which would have
 * rewritten it onto `/montavista/guides/` — was never invoked. Three attempts
 * to fix it inside the middleware failed for the same reason each time, and a
 * trace stamped onto every response returned nothing at all, which is what
 * finally said so.
 *
 * The proof is in the artifact: `dist/404.html` carried a canonical of
 * `/scipath/404/`, a path only build-time middleware could produce. The 404 a
 * reader saw was a build output, not a rendered page.
 *
 * With no file to serve, Cloudflare has to ask the worker, and the middleware
 * gets its turn.
 *
 * An earlier attempt at this was reverted, and the note left behind said why:
 * making this on demand makes every unmatched path on demand, and the
 * middleware then rewrote onto a prerendered route, which Astro forbids —
 * taking out every public page. That is no longer how it works. The
 * middleware fetches the file through the assets binding and returns it
 * directly; `next()` is a wrapped fallback rather than the mechanism, so a
 * refusal there reports itself instead of becoming a blank site.
 *
 * The cost is that a 404 is rendered rather than served from disk. It is one
 * page, it names no tenant, and it is the rarest response on the site.
 */
export const prerender = false;

import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Page not found" noindex>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="lost">
      <p class="t-lbl">404</p>
      <h1 class="t-big">That page is not here</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Either the address is wrong, or it pointed at something that has moved. Records
        published here keep their address permanently, so a broken link is usually a link
        from somewhere older.
      </p>

      <form class="sbar" action="/search/" method="get" role="search" style="margin-top:26px; max-width:520px">
        <label class="skip" for="q">Search records</label>
        <input class="in" type="search" id="q" name="q" />
        <button class="btn" type="submit">Search</button>
      </form>

      <div class="row" style="margin-top:20px">
        <a class="btn btn-2" href="/articles/">All records</a>
        <a class="btn btn-q" href="/guides/">Guides</a>
        <a class="btn btn-q" href="/">Home</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .lost {
    padding: 72px 0 60px;
    max-width: 74ch;
  }
  .lost .t-lbl {
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .lost .lede {
    margin-top: 18px;
  }
</style>
